{"chunk_id": "0280591d4f2f", "text": "After Rama\u2019s exile, the shock within the palace of Ayodhya deepens into catastrophe: King Dasaratha dies of grief. The royal women discover the lifeless king and collapse in anguish, their wailing filling the palace. Queen Kaushalya cradles his body and bitterly rebukes Kaikeyi, whose ambition forced Rama into exile and, in her view, destroyed the Raghu dynasty. She laments Rama and Sita wandering in the forest, imagines the grief of Sita\u2019s father Janaka, and even declares her intention to enter the funeral fire with her husband. Ministers intervene, preserving the king\u2019s body in oil until Rama or the princes can return. As news spreads, the palace and city sink into collective mourning: Ayodhya becomes like a moonless night, bereft of joy and leadership.\nAfter King Dasaratha\u2019s death, the queens and citizens of Ayodhya lament deeply while Kaushalya condemns Kaikeyi and ministers preserve the king\u2019s body until Rama returns.\nThemes: royal mourning, grief of queens, condemnation of Kaikeyi, death of Dasaratha, loyalty to Rama", "vector": [0.013363056816160679, -0.005524466745555401, -0.006082932930439711, -0.008534164167940617, -0.024599261581897736, 0.012359824031591415, -0.018660124391317368, -0.001363560208119452, -0.010955299250781536, -0.006410655565559864, 0.018325714394450188, 0.006236761808395386, 0.015904579311609268, 0.024599261581897736, -0.026164304465055466, 0.0058388132601976395, 0.04454352334141731, -0.002909374190494418, 0.036410652101039886, -0.010025637224316597, 0.009330062195658684, 0.0010742947924882174, -0.002713743830099702, 0.025227952748537064, -0.01642625965178013, 0.0018777168588712811, 0.012874817475676537, -0.03263849765062332, 0.01825883239507675, -0.00842046458274126, -0.0191684290766716, -0.01713521033525467, -0.0012615649029612541, -0.010527253150939941, -0.01693456433713436, 0.015209004282951355, -0.0010366735514253378, -0.00944376178085804, 0.015182252041995525, 0.008861